    "result_text": "Full suite is green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: `POST /api/owners` must record `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners sharing the new owner's `firstName` + `lastName` (case-insensitive) *before* this create \u2014 and return it on later reads (the test creates two same-named owners then `GET`s the second and expects `namesakeCount == 1`).\n\nSince the value is a create-time snapshot that must survive to a later `GET`, I persisted it rather than recomputing on read (recomputing would give a different, non-snapshot answer for the *first* owner).\n\nChanges, each in its natural place:\n\n1. **`CountNamesakes.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-responsibility OfficeFloor step that counts existing owners with a matching name via `OwnerRepository.findAll()` and stores it on the built owner. Runs after `BuildOwner`/`AssignHouseholdId` and before `SaveOwner`, so `findAll()` sees only the pre-existing owners.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `countNamesakes` step into the pipeline (`assignHousehold \u2192 countNamesakes \u2192 save`), under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbors.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a nullable `Integer namesakeCount` (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter, following the existing `customerCode`/`householdId` field pattern.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name automatically (no mapper change needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwner`/`RespondWithOwnerCreated` responders now emit it).\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the nullable `namesake_count` column so JPA `ddl-auto=none` matches the entity. Seed owners leave it null; only created owners get a value.\n\n`AcceptanceTest#coreCountsNamesakes` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
